# TCP vs UDP: Key Differences and Use Cases

## Core Differences

| Aspect | TCP | UDP |
|--------|-----|-----|
| **Connection** | Connection-oriented (3-way handshake) | Connectionless |
| **Reliability** | Guaranteed delivery, ordering, and integrity | Best-effort; no guarantees |
| **Error handling** | Retransmits lost packets, checksums | Checksums only; drops bad packets |
| **Ordering** | Packets reassembled in order | No ordering guarantee |
| **Flow/Congestion control** | Yes (windowing, slow start, etc
